{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a mild, triethylborane-initiated atom-transfer radical addition (ATRA) ring-opening of tricyclo[1.1.1.01,3]pentane (TCP) with alkyl halides to synthesize 1-halo-3-substituted bicyclo[1.1.1]pentanes (BCPs). These BCPs serve as bioisosteres for arenes and tert-butyl groups. The method demonstrates high functional group tolerance and is applied to the synthesis of BCP-modified nucleosides, peptides, and pharmaceuticals like fentanyl.",
